  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Khalid Hamid Hatture vs The State Of Maharashtra on 7 December, 2021 Author: V. G. Bisht Bench: V. G. Bisht 02-aba-2761-2021 . In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Anticipatory Bail Application No. 2761 Of 2021 Khalid Hamid Hatture ... Applica Versus The State of Maharashtra ... Respond Mr. Rahul B. Vijaymane, for the Applicant. Mr. Amit A. Palkar, App, for the State-Respondent. Coram : V. G. Bisht, J. Date : 7th December, 2021. Pc: The praecipe has been moved for the speaking to the minutes order dated 23rd November, 2021. 2 It seems that vide order dated 23 rd November, 2021, this Co continued the interim order granted earlier believing that there wa interim relief in favour of the applicant, however, it is not so. T",
    "facts": "The present application has been moved by the applicant under Section 438 of the Code of Criminal Procedure apprehending arrest under Sections 188, 272, 273, 328 read with 34 of the Indian Penal Code and Sections 26(2)(i), 26(2)(iv), 27(e) and Sec. 59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 registered vide C.R. No. 804 of 2021 with Solapur Police Station, District-Solapur. It appears that the applicant was found in possession Gutka,/Mava/Essence Tobacco/Essence Supari. However, having regard to the facts and circumstances of the case, prima facie applicability of Section 328 of the IPC appears to be doubtful. The applicant therefore has made out a case for ad-interim protection.",
